        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/vj052cw2158.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "crop 1, upper panel upright; pencil over the scanner's ruled lines. Number 1354, then a surname in a capital B and a run of minims that I cannot resolve and have not guessed, then the date. Day 1 and month 2 are plain. The year is 1 followed by a figure made of one descending curve closing into a single bowl on the baseline, with a short detached tick at its right: a 6 rather than the two-stroke 8 reading.md warns of, whose limbs would converge into a V above the bowl. No other 6 or 8 stands on the line to compare, so the 8 cannot be ruled out entirely."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
